CliPP2 is an independent, self-contained project licensed under AGPL-3.0;
see LICENSE. Its kernel and interfaces are maintained in this repository.
No CliPP1.5 installation, sibling checkout or network access is required.

Algorithm/source attribution:
The scalar binomial-multiplicity likelihood, pooled initializer, conditional
refits, mixture-weight optimization, chain continuation and candidate-search
algorithms were adapted from CliPP1.5 by its contributors, at commit
9e51e30ac8b0c8c9ab1f46821b496909843bda0c (AGPL-3.0):
https://github.com/yuadamding/CliPP1.5

CliPP2 maintains its own multi-region model, vector-tree continuation, native
N-by-R forest QP, in-memory chain ABI, selection adapters, validation and output
contract. These adapted sources are not represented as byte-identical upstream
files or as the complete CliPP1.5 API. Reference comparisons use the separate
CliPP1.5 repository only in external development tests.
